Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: avoid protocol-error backoff for local nexthop failures

TCP may connect before bgpd has received the local interface address or
IPv6 link-local address from zebra. bgp_getsockname() validates that local
nexthop state, not a received BGP packet. Sending an FSM-error NOTIFY for
this local failure needlessly doubles the start timer, up to 120 seconds.

Close through bgp_stop() and return failure without a NOTIFY in both the
normal and DelayOpen paths. Preserve deletion results for accepted and
dynamic peers. Keep the detailed EC_BGP_NH_UPD log from bgp_getsockname();
do not report a socket errno for a local nexthop-validation failure.

This is a recovery/backoff fix, not proof or repair of a stale-address
cache, a missed zebra update, or TCP connections remaining in SYN-SENT.
It preserves address validation, configured timers and protocol-error
backoff; it does not introduce immediate retries.

The regression exercises the real FSM with missing IPv4/IPv6 local
addresses, missing IPv6 link-local state, six repeated failures followed
by address readiness, Connect/Active, normal/DelayOpen, configured,
accepted and dynamic peers. Check socket closure, zero NOTIFY packets,
restart-timer preservation, successful OPEN processing after readiness,
and retained backoff for a received protocol notification.

Validation commands (FRR 10.7.1 plus the preceding SONiC patch series):
  make -j4 bgpd/bgpd tests/bgpd/test_local_nexthop tests/bgpd/test_peer_attr
  cd tests
  PYTHONPATH=helpers/python python3 -m pytest -q \
    bgpd/test_local_nexthop.py bgpd/test_peer_attr.py
Result: 196 passed. Removing the production fix makes the same regression
fail the unchanged-start-timer assertion.

---
diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_fsm.c b/bgpd/bgp_fsm.c
index d305d98..102a874 100644
--- a/bgpd/bgp_fsm.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_fsm.c
@@ -2460,6 +2460,18 @@ static void bgp_connect_check(struct event *event)
 	}
 }
 
+static enum bgp_fsm_state_progress
+bgp_connect_nexthop_error(struct peer_connection *connection)
+{
+	enum bgp_fsm_state_progress ret;
+
+	/* Local address readiness is not a peer protocol error. Close without
+	 * NOTIFY and its restart backoff, including accepted/dynamic peers.
+	 */
+	ret = bgp_stop(connection);
+	return ret == BGP_FSM_SUCCESS ? BGP_FSM_FAILURE : ret;
+}
+
 /* TCP connection open.  Next we send open message to remote peer. And
    add read thread for reading open message. */
 static enum bgp_fsm_state_progress
@@ -2473,15 +2485,8 @@ bgp_connect_success(struct peer_connection *connection)
 		return bgp_stop(connection);
 	}
 
-	if (bgp_getsockname(connection) < 0) {
-		flog_err_sys(EC_LIB_SOCKET,
-			     "%s: bgp_getsockname(): failed for peer %s, fd %d",
-			     __func__, peer->host, connection->fd);
-		bgp_notify_send(connection, BGP_NOTIFY_FSM_ERR,
-				bgp_fsm_error_subcode(connection->status));
-		bgp_writes_on(connection);
-		return BGP_FSM_FAILURE;
-	}
+	if (bgp_getsockname(connection) < 0)
+		return bgp_connect_nexthop_error(connection);
 
 	/*
 	 * If we are doing nht for a peer that ls v6 LL based
@@ -2524,15 +2529,8 @@ bgp_connect_success_w_delayopen(struct peer_connection *connection)
 		return bgp_stop(connection);
 	}
 
-	if (bgp_getsockname(connection) < 0) {
-		flog_err_sys(EC_LIB_SOCKET,
-			     "%s: bgp_getsockname(): failed for peer %s, fd %d",
-			     __func__, peer->host, connection->fd);
-		bgp_notify_send(connection, BGP_NOTIFY_FSM_ERR,
-				bgp_fsm_error_subcode(connection->status));
-		bgp_writes_on(connection);
-		return BGP_FSM_FAILURE;
-	}
+	if (bgp_getsockname(connection) < 0)
+		return bgp_connect_nexthop_error(connection);
 
 	/*
 	 * If we are doing nht for a peer that ls v6 LL based
